</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"4613" data-end=3D"4616" class=3D"">
<h3 data-start=3D"4618" data-end=3D"4661" class=3D"">2.2 Les constructeurs =
et les propri=C3=A9t=C3=A9s</h3>
<p data-start=3D"4663" data-end=3D"4851" class=3D"">Le <strong data-start=
=3D"4666" data-end=3D"4682">constructeur</strong> permet d'initialiser les =
propri=C3=A9t=C3=A9s d'un objet lors de sa cr=C3=A9ation. Dans l'exemple pr=
=C3=A9c=C3=A9dent, nous avons initialis=C3=A9 les propri=C3=A9t=C3=A9s <cod=
e data-start=3D"4814" data-end=3D"4820">name</code> et <code data-start=3D"=
4824" data-end=3D"4829">age</code> dans le constructeur.</p>
<h4 data-start=3D"4853" data-end=3D"4904" class=3D"">Propri=C3=A9t=C3=A9s <=
code data-start=3D"4869" data-end=3D"4877">public</code>, <code data-start=
=3D"4879" data-end=3D"4888">private</code>, et <code data-start=3D"4893" da=
ta-end=3D"4904">protected</code></h4>
<p data-start=3D"4906" data-end=3D"4976" class=3D"">En TypeScript, vous pou=
vez d=C3=A9finir la <strong data-start=3D"4944" data-end=3D"4958">visibilit=
=C3=A9</strong> d=E2=80=99une propri=C3=A9t=C3=A9 :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"4978" data-end=3D"5225">
<li data-start=3D"4978" data-end=3D"5064" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4980" data-end=3D"5064" class=3D""><code data-start=3D"498=
0" data-end=3D"4988">public</code> : la propri=C3=A9t=C3=A9 est accessible =
depuis l'ext=C3=A9rieur de la classe (par d=C3=A9faut).</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"5065" data-end=3D"5145" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"5067" data-end=3D"5145" class=3D""><code data-start=3D"506=
7" data-end=3D"5076">private</code> : la propri=C3=A9t=C3=A9 est accessible=
 uniquement =C3=A0 l'int=C3=A9rieur de la classe.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"5146" data-end=3D"5225" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"5148" data-end=3D"5225" class=3D""><code data-start=3D"514=
8" data-end=3D"5159">protected</code> : la propri=C3=A9t=C3=A9 est accessib=
le dans la classe et ses sous-classes.</p>
</li>
</ul>
