<h3 data-start=3D"2105" data-end=3D"2133" class=3D"">Qu=E2=80=99est-ce que =
le scope ?</h3>
<p data-start=3D"2135" data-end=3D"2231" class=3D"">Le <strong data-start=
=3D"2138" data-end=3D"2147">scope</strong> d=E2=80=99un service d=C3=A9sign=
e la <strong data-start=3D"2172" data-end=3D"2206">port=C3=A9e de visibilit=
=C3=A9 et de vie</strong> de l=E2=80=99instance inject=C3=A9e :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"2233" data-end=3D"2362">
<li data-start=3D"2233" data-end=3D"2294" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"2235" data-end=3D"2294" class=3D"">Scope global =E2=86=92 =
Une seule instance partag=C3=A9e dans toute l=E2=80=99app</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2295" data-end=3D"2362" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"2297" data-end=3D"2362" class=3D"">Scope local =E2=86=92 U=
ne instance propre =C3=A0 un module, un composant, etc.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<blockquote data-start=3D"2364" data-end=3D"2434">
<p data-start=3D"2366" data-end=3D"2434" class=3D"">Angular permet de d=C3=
=A9finir ce scope pr=C3=A9cis=C3=A9ment via les <code data-start=3D"2421" d=
ata-end=3D"2433">injecteurs</code>.</p>
</blockquote>
